    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Para processar um CSV em blocos de 10000 linhas, use o parâmetro `chunksize=10000` na função `pandas.read_csv`. Isso permite que os dados sejam lidos em partes, reduzindo o uso de memória. O parâmetro `chunksize` é opcional e especifica o número de linhas por bloco. A leitura ocorre em chunks, permitindo processar grandes arquivos sem carregá-los completamente na memória.",
        "evidence_ids": [
          "4930995f0c04f0d496ed6144",
          "0c34bda3ca03adedf9827a8c"
        ],
        "evidence_quotes": [
          {
            "source_id": "4930995f0c04f0d496ed6144",
            "quote": "\\\nSuppose you wish to iterate through a (potentially very large) file lazily\\\nrather than reading the entire file into memory, such as the following:\\\n\\\n```\\\nIn [224]: df = pd.DataFrame(np.random.randn(10, 4))\\\n\\\nIn [225]: df.to_csv(\"tmp.csv\", index=False)\\\n\\\nIn [226]: table = pd.read_csv(\"tmp.csv\")\\\n\\\nIn [227]: table\\\nOut[227]:\\\n          0         1         2         3\\\n0 -1.294524  0.413738  0.276662 -0.472035\\\n1 -0.013960 -0.362543 -0.006154 -0.923061\\\n2  0.895717  0.805244 -1.206412  2.565646\\\n3  1.431256  1.340309 -1.170299 -0.226169\\\n4  0.410835  0.813850  0.132003 -0.827317\\\n5 -0.076467 -1.187678  1.130127 -1.436737\\\n6 -1.413681  1.607920  1.024180  0.569605\\\n7  0.875906 -2.211372  0.974466 -2.006747\\\n8 -0.410001 -0.078638  0.545952 -1.219217\\\n9 -1.226825  0.769804 -1.281247 -0.727707\\\n```\\\n\\\nCopy to clipboard\\\n\\\nBy specifying a `chunksize` to `read_csv`, the return\\"
          },
          {
            "source_id": "0c34bda3ca03adedf9827a8c",
            "quote": "chunksize int, optional\n\nNumber of lines to read from the file per chunk. Passing a value will cause the\nfunction to return a `TextFileReader` object for iteration.\nSee the IO Tools docs\nfor more information on `iterator` and `chunksize`."
          }
        ]
      }
